{"canManage() method treats AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW as sufficient for global group management by calling hasPermission(null, AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE) - VIEW should not confer create/move authority": 0.9460886120796204, "getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() uses groupResource.getId() (authorization resource IDs) instead of groupResource.getName() (Keycloak group IDs), causing permission checks to miss intended per-group resources and returning UUIDs that downstream group filters cannot match": 0.8138415217399597, "requireManageMembers() Javadoc points at canManage() but should point at canManageMembership(GroupModel)": 0.38600394129753113, "@return tags say Stream but the method returns Set<String>": 0.16493090987205505, "canMapRole() checks root.hasOneAdminRole(AdminRoles.MANAGE_USERS) then calls checkAdminRoles(role), removing the schema-level users-manage shortcut - should return true immediately when MANAGE_USERS is detected": 0.40280842781066895, "UserPermissionsV2 dropped the AdminRoles.ADMIN fast-path shortcut - users granted only the umbrella admin role will fail canView/canManage/canMapRoles/canManageGroupMembership checks": 0.6794227957725525, "AdminPermissions listener for cleanup on role/client/group removal is only registered when ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ is enabled, leaving orphaned authorization state in V2-only deployments": 0.35061872005462646, "response.getLocation() can be null even with 201 status, causing NPE - should add explicit null assertion before parsing the path": 0.1255972981452942, "RealmAdminPermissionsConfig adds AdminRoles.QUERY_GROUPS to shared fixture, which may hide regressions in Groups resource-type permission path for tests that shouldn't satisfy the group list gate": 0.39535027742385864}